  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Neeraj Kumar vs Commissioner Of Food Safety And ... on 30 November, 2022 Author: Vivek Chaudhary Bench: Vivek Chaudhary High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 4 Case :- Matters Under Article 227 No. - 10902 of 2022 Petitioner :- Neeraj Kumar Respondent :- Commissioner Of Food Safety And Principal Secretary And 3 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- Sushil Kumar Sharma,Abhishe Pandey",
    "facts": "The instant petition has been filed by the petitioner challenging the order dated 31.10.2022 passed by District Judge, Moradabad in Regular Civil Appeal No. 173 of 2022 (Neeraj Kumar vs. State), under Section 51 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, by which appeal of the petitioner was admitted and conditional stay was granted to deposit 50% fine within one month. It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner that the Additional District Magistrate (Administration), Moradabad without considering the objection of the petitioner had imposed a very excessive fine of Rs.3,00,000/- vide order dated 31.08.2022 and the appellate court while admitting the appeal has directed to deposit 50% of the fine ordered by the Additional District Magistrate (Administration), Moradabad. Neeraj Kumar vs Commissioner Of Food Safety And ... on 30 November, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/168973012/",
